@startuml geo-cell-write
title US-12: Geo-Cell Write - Two H3 Resolutions: HISTORY for TimescaleDB, LIVE for Redis sorted sets

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:{cell_id}\n(sorted set)" as GeoCell

Kafka -> Consumer : consume event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

Consumer -> Consumer : compute H3 cell IDs:\nhistory_cell = h3.latLngToCell(lat, lon, HISTORY_H3_RESOLUTION)\nlive_cell    = h3.latLngToCell(lat, lon, LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION)

note over Consumer
  HISTORY_H3_RESOLUTION — configurable:
    used for TimescaleDB geo_cell index column.
    Larger cells = fewer distinct values = better index selectivity
    for bounding-box queries over historical windows.
  LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION — configurable, tuned independently:
    used for Redis sorted sets (geo-cell proximity index).
    Smaller cells = tighter spatial locality
    for proximity k-ring expansion.
  If both resolutions are equal, only one cell ID is computed.
  Tune both during implementation based on entity density
  and PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES.
end note

Consumer -> TSDB : INSERT INTO position_history\n(\n  entity_id,\n  geo_cell,        -- history_geo_cell (HISTORY_H3_RESOLUTION)\n  observed_at,     -- to_timestamp(timestamp_ms/1000.0)\n  timestamp_ms,    -- source fidelity + logical idempotency key\n  lat, lon, altitude\n)\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, observed_at) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Hypertable partitioned by observed_at (TIMESTAMPTZ).
  geo_cell is an ordinary indexed column, not a partition dimension.
  Queries filter on geo_cell IN ($cells) AND observed_at BETWEEN $t1 AND $t2.
  TimescaleDB chunk exclusion applies to the time dimension only.
end note

Consumer -> GeoCell : ZADD geo-cell:{live_cell} $timestamp_ms $entity_id
note over GeoCell
  Score = last_seen_ms.
  Correlation Worker queries with ZRANGEBYSCORE
  to filter out stale members before proximity check.
  LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION cells are smaller, giving
  tighter k-ring expansion at proximity detection time.
end note

@enduml
